        <!-- news feed -->
          <table style="width:100%;border:0px;border-spacing:0px;border-collapse:separate;margin-right:auto;margin-left:auto;">
            <tbody>
              <tr>
              <td style="padding-left:2.5%;padding-bottom:20px;width:100%;vertical-align:middle">
                <heading><b>News</b></heading>
                <p>
                  <ul class="fa-ul">
                    <li> <img src="images/new_animated.gif" \=""> <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[Oct 2026] </p> I'm honored to be named a <a href="https://www.schmidtsciences.org/ai2050-fellows-2026-announcement/">2026 AI2050 Early Career Fellow</a> by Schmidt Sciences!</li>
                    <li> <img src="images/new_animated.gif" \=""> <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[Sept 2026] </p> We have 5 papers accepted to CoRL! Find the links here: <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.00267">StressDream</a>, <a href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2606.14981">Steering via Vision & Touch</a>, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.12299">Learning What to Say to Your VLA</a>, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.06492">Do World Models Understand Partially Observable Safety Constraints?</a>, and <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.31132">Scaling Test-Time Compute in Robotics</a>.</li>
                    <li> <img src="images/new_animated.gif" \=""> <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[Aug 2026] </p> I gave a talk at <a href="https://robotics.gatech.edu/seminars">Georgia Tech's Robotics Colloquium</a>!</li>
                    <li> <i class="fa fa-chevron-right"\></i> <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[July 2026] </p>New arXiv paper on <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.31132"><i>ELASTIC</i></a>: adapting test-time compute for generative control policies.</li>
                    <li> <i class="fa fa-chevron-right"\></i> <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[June 2026] </p>I gave a Keynote talk at the <a href="https://summer-school.rpl.eecs.kth.se/programme/">RPL Summer School on Robot Learning</a> in Sweden 🇸🇪.</li>
                    <li> <i class="fa fa-chevron-right"\></i> <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[June 2026] </p>New arXiv paper on <a href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2606.14981"><i>ViTaL</i></a>: visuo-tactile inference-time policy steering.</li>
                    <li> <i class="fa fa-chevron-right"\></i> <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[June 2026] </p>New arXiv paper on <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.13672"><i>WEAVER</i></a>: a better, faster, and longer-horizon world model for manipulation. The pre-trained model and codebase is open-sourced too <a href="https://arnavkj1995.github.io/WEAVER/">here</a>. </li>
                    <li> <i class="fa fa-chevron-right"\></i> <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[June 2026] </p>New <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.12299">arXiv paper</a> on learning a language feedback policy that steers a frozen VLA; the policy learns what to say to the VLA and (crucially) when not to say anything.</li>
                    <li> <i class="fa fa-chevron-right"\></i> <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[June 2026] </p>New arXiv paper on <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.00267"><i>StressDream</i></a>: a noise optimization algorithm for steering pre-trained video world models. Check out how StressDream can help with robust policy evaluation and improvement <a href="https://junwon.me/StressDream/">here</a>.</li>
                    <li> <i class="fa fa-chevron-right"\></i> <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[May 2026] </p>New arXiv paper on <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.11485"><i>Coordinated Diffusion</i></a>: an algorithm for generating multi-agent robot behavior without multi-agent demonstrations.</li>
                    <li> <i class="fa fa-chevron-right"\></i> <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[May 2026] </p>I gave a <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mFh1hXyth-o&list=PLTPQEx-31JXglBI77fRlkAngwUUExSL-n&index=2">talk</a> at the University of Washington's Robotics Colloquium!</li>
                    <li> <i class="fa fa-chevron-right"\></i> <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[April 2026] </p>Our <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.01036">position paper</a> on reward modeling was accepted as a spotlight to ICML (top 5%)!</li>
                    <li> <i class="fa fa-chevron-right"\></i> <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[April 2026] </p>Our <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.22474">paper</a> on uncertainty-aware policy steering was accepted to RSS!</li>
                    <li> <i class="fa fa-chevron-right"\></i>  <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[March 2026] </p>New <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.22474">arXiv paper</a> on uncertainty-aware policy steering.</li>
                    <li> <i class="fa fa-chevron-right"\></i>  <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[Jan 2026] </p>Three papers accepted to ICRA! Check out the <a href="https://cmu-intentlab.github.io/publications.html">publications</a> on the lab website.</li>
                    <li> <i class="fa fa-chevron-right"\></i>  <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[Jan 2026] </p>One paper on <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.18606">latent CBFs</a> accepted to L4DC as an oral talk!</li>
                  </ul>

                  <!-- OLDER NEWS -->
                  <ul class="fa-ul">
                    <p style="color:black;">
                    <button class="button1" onclick="myFunction()"><p style="color:black;"><i class="fa fa-chevron-down" aria-hidden="true"></i> [Older News]</p></button>
                    </p>

                    <div id="last_name_button" style="display:none;">
                    <li> <i class="fa fa-chevron-right"\></i>  <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[Dec 2025] </p>One paper on <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.13727">control-theoretic LLM guardrails</a> accepted to the International Association for Safe and Ethical AI!</li>
                    <li> <i class="fa fa-chevron-right"\></i> <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[Nov 2025] </p>New arXiv paper on <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.18606">latent-space control barrier functions</a> for visuomotor policy safety.</li>
                    <li> <i class="fa fa-chevron-right"\></i> <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[Nov 2025] </p>Honored to receive the <a href="https://www.amazon.science/research-areas/latest-news/63-amazon-research-award-recipients-announced-spring-2025">Amazon Research Award</a>!</li>
                    <li> <i class="fa fa-chevron-right"\></i> <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[Oct 2025] </p>I gave a talk at <a href="https://ivado.ca/en/">IVADO</a> Workshop on Assessing & Improving Agent Capabilities & Safety. Titled <i>From Refusal to Recovery: Control-Theoretic Approach to Agent Guardrails</i> and you can check it out on <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7J9tPVNtunU">YouTube</a>!</li>
                    <li> <i class="fa fa-chevron-right"\></i> <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[Oct 2025]  </p>Four new arXiv papers! We studied how <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.06492">latent-space safe control can go wrong under partially observable constraints</a> but <i>multimodal data</i> is a promising remedy, how to <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.19555">adapt latent safety filters at runtime</a> with images of constraints, how we can automatically <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.13727">compute agentic AI guardrails</a> by performing control-theoretic optimization directly on LLM agent models, and how we can <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.16281">steer VLAs at runtime</a> by verifying that their intermediate reasoning steps actually align with the outcomes of their actions. </li>
                    <li> <i class="fa fa-chevron-right"\></i> <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[Sept 2025]  </p>I'm honored to receive the <a href="https://www.darpa.mil/work-with-us/communities/academia/young-faculty-award">DARPA Young Faculty Award (YFA)</a>! </li>
                    <li> <i class="fa fa-chevron-right"\></i> <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[Aug 2025]  </p>Two papers accepted to CoRL! One on <a href="http://arxiv.org/abs/2505.00779">controlling away from known and out-of-distribution failures</a> and one on <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.12678">out-of-distribution adaptation at runtime via "analogy"</a>. </li>
                    <li> <i class="fa fa-chevron-right"\></i>  <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[May 2025]  </p>Check out the Robotics Institute's <a href="https://www.ri.cmu.edu/andrea-bajcsy-earns-nsf-career-award/">article</a> about my CAREER award and our initial results. </li>
                    <li> <i class="fa fa-chevron-right"\></i>  <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[May 2025]  </p>New paper on arXiv on <a href="http://arxiv.org/abs/2505.00779">uncertainty-aware latent safety filters</a> which proactively steer robots away from both known and out-of-distribution failures.</li>
                    <li> <i class="fa fa-chevron-right"\></i>  <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[May 2025]  </p>We ran a successful 2nd edition of the <a href="https://nescw.org/">Northeast Systems and Control Workshop</a>! </li>
                    <li> <i class="fa fa-chevron-right"\></i>  <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[April 2025]  </p>Honored to receive the <a href="https://www.nsf.gov/awardsearch/showAward?AWD_ID=2441014&HistoricalAwards=false">NSF CAREER Award</a>!</li>
                    <li> <i class="fa fa-chevron-right"\></i>  <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[April 2025]  </p>Two papers accepted at RSS! Check them out <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2502.00935">here</a> and <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2502.01828">here</a>. 
                    <li> <i class="fa fa-chevron-right"\></i> <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[March 2025]  </p>Check out my <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wwRYUbpphMw&list=PLCFD85BC79FE703DF&index=6">talk</a> titled "Towards Open World Robot Safety" at the RI Seminar!</li>
                    <li> <i class="fa fa-chevron-right"\></i> <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[Feb 2025]  </p>Two new arXiv papers: <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2502.00935">latent-space reachability</a> for generalizing safety beyond collision-avoidance and <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2502.01828">VLM-in-the-loop policy steering</a>!</li>
                    <li> <i class="fa fa-chevron-right"\></i> <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[Jan 2025]  </p>Two accepted papers (<a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2409.14580">updating safety via language</a> and <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2409.12153">safely influencing</a>) at ICRA 2025!</li>
                    <li> <i class="fa fa-chevron-right"\></i> <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[Jan 2025]  </p>One <a href="http://arxiv.org/abs/2410.08852">accepted paper</a> on conformalized IL at ICLR 2025!</li>
                    <li> <i class="fa fa-chevron-right"\></i> <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[Jan 2025]  </p>We are running two workshops at ICRA! One on <a href="https://sites.google.com/stanford.edu/safe-vlm-icra/home">Safely Leveraging VLMs in Robotics</a> and the other on <a href="https://saferobotics.princeton.edu/ptas-icra25">Public Trust in Autonomy</a></li>
                    <li><i class="fa fa-chevron-right"\></i> <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[Oct 2024]  </p>New <a href="http://arxiv.org/abs/2410.08852">arXiv paper</a> on conformal prediction + interactive imitation learning.</li>
                    <li><i class="fa fa-chevron-right"\></i> <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[Sept 2024]  </p> Three new arXiv papers! Check out our work on <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2409.09883">robots that suggest safe alternatives</a>, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2409.14580">updating robot safety representations online from natural language</a>, and <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2409.12153">robots that learn to safely influence</a>.</li>
                    <li><i class="fa fa-chevron-right"\></i> <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[Sept 2024]  </p> New <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2403.04745">paper</a> accepted to CoRL on how not all prediction errors are made equal from the perspective of closed-loop robot performance.</li>
                    <li><i class="fa fa-chevron-right"\></i> <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[Aug 2024]  </p> New <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2312.06653">paper</a> at ECCV on adapting human trajectory predictors to scene-specific behaviors.</li>
                    <li><i class="fa fa-chevron-right"\></i> <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[June 2024]  </p> New <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.09794">arXiv paper</a> on human--AI safety through the lens of generative AI and control systems.</li>
                    <li><i class="fa fa-chevron-right"\></i> <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[Apr 2024]  </p> New <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2406.07767">paper</a> at RSS on using conformal prediction to calibrated shared controllers.</li>
                    <li><i class="fa fa-chevron-right"\></i> <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[Apr 2024]  </p> I'm thrilled to receive the <a href="https://research.google/programs-and-events/research-scholar-program/recipients/">Google Research Scholar Award</a>!</li>
                    <li><i class="fa fa-chevron-right"\></i><p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[Mar 2024]  </p> New <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2403.04745">arXiv paper</a> on a general calibrated regret metric for detecting and mitigating human-robot interaction failures; check out the applicability to anomaly detection in interactive generative planners too!</li>
                      <li><i class="fa fa-chevron-right"\></i>  <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[Feb 2024]  </p> New <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2402.10182">arXiv paper</a> on intent demonstration in general-sum dynamic games. </li>
                      <li><i class="fa fa-chevron-right"\></i> <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[Jan 2024]  </p> Our work on <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2310.07932">visual representation alignment for robot learning</a> was accepted to ICLR 2024! Check out the new results in the arXiv version.</li>
                      <li><i class="fa fa-chevron-right"\></i> <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[Jan 2024]  </p> Our work on <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2304.05483">contingency games</a> was accepted to RA-L 2024!</li>
                      <li><i class="fa fa-chevron-right"\></i> <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[Jan 2024]  </p> Our work on <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2308.09863">stabilized and robust online learning from humans</a> was accepted to RA-L 2024!</li>
                      <li><i class="fa fa-chevron-right"\></i> <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[Dec 2023]  </p> New <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2312.06653">pre-print</a> on Adaptive Human Trajectory Prediction via Latent Corridors.</li>
                      <li><i class="fa fa-chevron-right"\></i> <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[Oct 2023]  </p> Submitted a <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2310.07932">paper</a> to ICLR! We propose <i>Representation-Aligned Preference-based Learning (RAPL)</i>, a tractable video-only method for solving the visual representation alignment problem and learning visual robot rewards via optimal transport. </li>
                      <li><i class="fa fa-chevron-right"\></i> <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[Sep 2023]  </p> Submitted a <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2310.05921">paper</a> to ICRA! We present Conformal Decision Theory, a new theoretical and algorithmic framework for online calibration of decision risk.</li>
                      <li><i class="fa fa-chevron-right"\></i> <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[Aug 2023]  </p> ArXiv <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2308.16185">paper</a> on learning vision-based pursuit-evasion robot policies. Check out our <a href="https://abajcsy.github.io/vision-based-pursuit/">project website</a> for videos of human-robot and robot-robot interaction ``in the wild''.</li>
                      <li><i class="fa fa-chevron-right"\></i> <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[Aug 2023]  </p> 1 paper accepted to CoRL! <a href="https://saferoboticslab.github.io/Belief-Game/">This work</a> synthesizes safe control policies that explicitly account a robot's ability to learn and adapt at runtime.</li> 
                      <li><i class="fa fa-chevron-right"\></i> <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[Aug 2023]</p> Submitted a <a href="https://collab.me.vt.edu/pdfs/shaunak_ral2023.pdf">paper</a> to RA-L on stabilized and robust online learning from humans.</li>
                      <li><i class="fa fa-chevron-right"\></i> <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[Aug 2023]</p> Extended results on contingency games now on <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2304.05483">arXiv</a>.</li>
                      <li><i class="fa fa-chevron-right"\></i> <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[Aug 2023]</p> I gave a talk at  <a href="https://www.bosch.us/our-company/innovation/">Bosch</a> research.</li>
                      <li><i class="fa fa-chevron-right"\></i> <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[Apr 2023]</p> New <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2304.05483">paper</a> on <i>contingency games</i>: a model for strategic interactions which allows a robot to consider the full distribution of other agents’ intents while anticipating intent certainty in the near future.</li>
                      <li><i class="fa fa-chevron-right"\></i> <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[Feb 2023]</p> I gave a talk at the <a href="https://robotics.illinois.edu/robotics-seminar-series/">Illinois Robotics Seminar</a> at UIUC.</li>
                    <li><i class="fa fa-chevron-right"\></i> <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[Feb 2023]</p> I gave a talk at the <a href="https://robotics.wisc.edu/seminar-series/">Wisconsin Robotics Seminar Series</a> at the University of Wisconsin-Madison.</li>
                      <li><i class="fa fa-chevron-right"\></i> <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[Jan 2023]</p> Our <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2209.10588">paper</a> on long-term robot influence on humans got accepted to ICRA 2023!</li>
                      <li><i class="fa fa-chevron-right"\></i> <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[Jan 2023]</p> Our paper on <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2301.00901">modeling & influencing the dynamics of human learning</a> was accepted to HRI 2023! </li>
                      <li><i class="fa fa-chevron-right"></i> <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[Dec 2022]</p> I am on the organizing committee of <a href="https://roboticsconference.org/">RSS 2023</a>.</li>
                      <li><i class="fa fa-chevron-right"></i> <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[Dec 2022]</p> I gave a guest lecture at Princeton's <a href="https://mobile.princeton.edu/default/courses/detail?area=ECE&course=002543&term=1222">Safety-Critical Robotic Systems</a> class.</li>
                      <li><i class="fa fa-chevron-right"></i> <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[Nov 2022]</p> I am serving as an Area Chair for <a href="https://l4dc.seas.upenn.edu/">L4DC</a>.</li>
                      <li><i class="fa fa-chevron-right"></i> <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[Oct 2022]</p> I gave an invited talk at <a href="https://www.nuro.ai/">Nuro</a> on practical safety for human-robot interaction.</li>
                      <li><i class="fa fa-chevron-right"></i> <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[Sept 2022]</p> <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2209.10588">Paper</a> submitted to ICRA on robots that influence humans over long-term interaction.</li>
                      <li><i class="fa fa-chevron-right"></i> <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[Sept 2022]</p> I'm serving as Associate Editor for ICRA 2023.</li>
                      
                      <li><i class="fa fa-chevron-right"></i> <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[Aug 2022]</p> I completed my PhD and started my postdoc! My thesis entitled <i>"Bridging Safety and Learning in Human-Robot Interaction"</i> can be found <a href="https://www2.eecs.berkeley.edu/Pubs/TechRpts/2022/EECS-2022-181.html">here</a>.</li>

                      <li><i class="fa fa-chevron-right"></i> <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[July 2022]</p> I gave an invited talk at the ICML Workshop on <a href="https://learn-to-race.org/workshop-sl4ad-icml2022/">Safe Learning for Autonomous Driving (SL4AD)</a>.</li>
                      
                      <li><i class="fa fa-chevron-right"></i> <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[June 2022]</p> I gave an invited talk at the RSS Workshop on <a href="https://sites.google.com/colorado.edu/rss-22-close-proximity-hrc/schedule?authuser=0">Close Proximity Human-Robot Collaboration</a>.</li>

                      <li><i class="fa fa-chevron-right"></i> <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[May 2022]</p> I accepted an offer to join the <a href="https://www.ri.cmu.edu">Robotics Institute</a> in the <a href="https://www.cs.cmu.edu/">School of Computer Science</a> at <a href="https://www.cmu.edu/">Carnegie Mellon University (CMU)</a> starting Fall 2023!</li>

                      <li><i class="fa fa-chevron-right"></i> <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[Mar 2022]</p> Our paper <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2109.14700">Safety Assurances for Human-Robot Interaction via Confidence-aware Game-theoretic Human Models</a> was accepted to ICRA 2022! </li>

                      <li><i class="fa fa-chevron-right"></i> <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[Nov 2021]</p> I gave a talk at the University of Washington's <a href="https://robotics.cs.washington.edu/colloquium/">Robotics Colloqium</a>. </li>

                      <li><i class="fa fa-chevron-right" aria-hidden="true"></i> <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[Oct 2021]</p> <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2107.02349">Paper</a> published in IJRR! In this work we formalize how physical human interaction with a robot can be treated as a form of communication, enabling robots to learn objectives from human corrections.</li>

                      <li><i class="fa fa-chevron-right" aria-hidden="true"></i> <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[Oct 2021]</p> New <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2109.14700">paper</a> on arXiv! In this work we propose that robots use confidence-aware game-theoretic models of human behavior when assessing the safety of a human-robot interaction.</li>
                     <!-- <p style="color:black;padding-top: 0px"> <i class="fa fa-arrow-circle-right" aria-hidden="true"></i> Sounds like &nbsp <b>BYE-chee</b></p> -->
                      <li><i class="fa fa-chevron-right" aria-hidden="true"></i> <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[Aug 2021]</p> I am grateful to have been selected for the <a href="https://risingstars21-eecs.mit.edu/">Rising Stars Academic Career Workshop in EECS</a>.</li>

                      <li><i class="fa fa-chevron-right" aria-hidden="true"></i> <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[Aug 2021]</p> New <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2107.14412">paper</a> on arXiv! In this work we advocate for the use of Hamilton Jacobi (HJ) reachability as a unifying mathematical framework for comparing existing safety concepts used throughout industry and academia, and propose ways to expand its modeling premises in a data-driven fashion.</li>

                      <li><i class="fa fa-chevron-right" aria-hidden="true"></i> <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[April 2021]</p> I'm excited to join NVIDIA for an internship in the Autonomous Driving Research group led by <a href="https://research.nvidia.com/person/marco-pavone">Marco Pavone</a>.</li>

                      <li><i class="fa fa-chevron-right" aria-hidden="true"></i> <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[Mar 2021]</p> Our paper on <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2103.05746">analyzing human models that adapt online</a> was accepted to ICRA 2021!</li>

                      <li><i class="fa fa-chevron-right"></i> <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[Feb 2021]</p> I gave a talk at University of Pennsylvania on analyzing human models that adapt online. </li>

                      <li><i class="fa fa-chevron-right"></i> <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[Dec 2020]</p> I gave a talk on safe robots which learn from (and about) humans at the <a href="https://www.ucls.uchicago.edu/e-news-detail/~post/virtual-robots-and-long-distance-expertise-20201214">University of Chicago Laboratory School</a> for the middle and high-school robotics club.</li>

                      <li><i class="fa fa-chevron-right" aria-hidden="true"></i> <p style="display:inline;color:#f18800;">[Dec 2020]</p> I gave a <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=neEEKv0rXLc">talk</a> at <a href="https://idsc.ethz.ch/research-frazzoli/autonomy-talks.html">ETH Zurich</a> on introspective human motion prediction for safe robot autonomy.</li>
                      </div>

                      <script>
